/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Recognizing the transformative power of education as a catalyst for positive change, we launched Project Empower-ED, an initiative aimed at empowering underprivileged children through education. With a firm belief in the potential of every child to succeed, regardless of their socio-economic background, the project seeks to alleviate financial barriers and provide holistic support to ensure access to educational opportunities.)
/E (Recognizing the transformative power of education as a catalyst for positive change, we launched Project Empower-ED, an initiative aimed at empowering underprivileged children through education. With a firm belief in the potential of every child to succeed, regardless of their socio-economic background, the project seeks to alleviate financial barriers and provide holistic support to ensure access to educational opportunities.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
238 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The primary objective of Project Empower-ED is to break the cycle of poverty by equipping underprivileged children with the tools they need to excel academically and pursue their dreams. Through comprehensive scholarships, we aim to cover all educational expenses, including tuition fees, uniforms, books, examination fees, and other necessities. Additionally, the project endeavours to foster holistic development through sports, co-curricular activities, and educational excursions, enriching the educational experience and enhancing employability prospects.)
/E (The primary objective of Project Empower-ED is to break the cycle of poverty by equipping underprivileged children with the tools they need to excel academically and pursue their dreams. Through comprehensive scholarships, we aim to cover all educational expenses, including tuition fees, uniforms, books, examination fees, and other necessities. Additionally, the project endeavours to foster holistic development through sports, co-curricular activities, and educational excursions, enriching the educational experience and enhancing employability prospects.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
